From c60f633545ba8ed9bdcac5737fa33c47d54030cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:37:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 314/314] macro_rules: two optional repetitions that read the same tokens
 to the end take the loop

bindgen 0.72.1 (py314-qh3 2.0.4) features.rs:226:

    macro_rules! define_rust_targets {
        (
            Nightly => {$($nightly_feature:ident ..),* $(,)?} $(,)?
            $( $variant:ident($minor:literal) => {..}, )*
            $(,)?
        ) => { .. }
    }

    features.rs:226-309 BUG: src/macro_rules/parse.cpp:975: TODO: macro_pattern_to_simple_inner - Entry and skip
    patterns share an entry (max extend 2), ambigious - PAT_TOKEN:TOK_COMMA, PAT_TOKEN:TOK_EOF, PAT_TOKEN:TOK_EOF

The `$(,)?` after `Nightly => {..}` can take a comma that the trailing
`$(,)?` could take too when the repetition between them is empty: for `,`
and then the end, entering and skipping are the same condition, however far
the lookahead is extended, so the matcher wasn't built at all (smallest
shape: `A $(,)? $(,)?`). An end can only be matched at the end of the
pattern, so both ways read the same tokens and stop in the same place;
the loop is taken. (bindgen's comma is always followed by more variants.)

Kit macro-optional-twice-test (typeck, stand-in core): bindgen's macro and
invocation, `A $(,)? $( $v:ident, )* $(,)?` and the `),*` form with every
binding used; neg_three.rs: `A,,,` is an error, not a BUG. `A,` itself,
which both could read, is left out (rustc may call it ambiguous).

Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---

diff --git a/src/macro_rules/parse.cpp b/src/macro_rules/parse.cpp
index 5d05ec17..dada4763 100644
--- a/src/macro_rules/parse.cpp
+++ b/src/macro_rules/parse.cpp
@@ -972,6 +972,15 @@ namespace {
                             ambiguous = true;
                             break;
                         }
+                        // Both read the same tokens up to the end of the input (an end can only be matched at the end of
+                        // the pattern), so they end in the same place: take the loop. `A $(,)? $( $v:ident, )* $(,)?`
+                        // with `A,`: the trailing `$(,)?` could take the comma too (bindgen 0.72.1 features.rs:226
+                        // `define_rust_targets!`, where the comma is always followed by more variants)
+                        if( e_it->back().ty == MacroPatEnt::PAT_TOKEN && e_it->back().tok == TOK_EOF ) {
+                            DEBUG("Entry and skip both read " << *e_it << " to the end, take the loop");
+                            skip_conds.erase(s_it);
+                            continue;
+                        }
                         TODO(ent.sp, "Entry and skip patterns share an entry (max extend " << MAX_CONDITION_ADD << "), ambigious - " << *e_it);
                     }
                 }
